coder › Implemented `parseIni` in `src/ini.ts` and expanded `src/ini.test.ts`.

What changed:
- `src/ini.ts` — full parser:
  - Splits input on `\r\n`, `\n`, or `\r`; trims each line before classifying it.
  - Ignores blank lines and lines starting with `;` or `#` (leading whitespace allowed).
  - `[name]` lines switch the current section; whitespace around the name is trimmed, and keys before any header go under `''`.
  - Splits only on the first `=`, trims key and value, and strips surrounding double quotes only when the whole trimmed value is wrapped in them (preserving interior spaces and `;`).
  - Later keys overwrite earlier ones in the same section.
  - Anything else throws `SyntaxError: Invalid INI on line <n>` with the 1-based line number.
- `src/ini.test.ts` — added tests for the empty-string pre-section, whitespace trimming, comments/blank lines, quoted-value preservation, first-`=` splitting, override behavior, multiple sections, empty quoted value, and the SyntaxError line number.

